<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Bautista de Anza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1736">1736</a>–<a href="/years/1788">1788</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Bautista de Anza was a frontier officer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonora">Sonora</a>, who led overland expeditions to Alta <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> in 1774 and 1775–1776, bringing the settlers who founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a>. As governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> from 1778 to 1787 he defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> leader Cuerno Verde and made a lasting peace with the Comanche in 1786.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juan-bautista-de-anza.jpg" alt="Juan Bautista de Anza" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fray Orci · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Juan_Bautista_de_Anza_(Painted_by_Fray_Orci;_1774,_Mexico_City).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
